mantle rm243
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_orm_nailhand
title the weekly caller
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk identifies_ships_by_their_shadows
likes spiced_cider swimming fresh_straw warm_rain
dislikes deep_mud smoke
fears a_name_rubbed_off_the_roll
hopes a_receipt_for_the_petition
topics work +0.5 land +0.4 travel +0.3 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=practical gossip=brief refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# studies hull shadows, keeps a folded petition flat against the ribs and saves the plainest words for the hardest question.

words
oath! = Blot my copy | Smudge the seal
saying! = A slip of paper needs two legs | Even a shadow has a draught
copy = my folded copy | my clean copy
strawbit = a bright stalk | a stem of straw
prow = the lip of the bow | the rising end
receipt = a dated scrap | a mark of receipt
ripple = the split in the water | the narrow wake
bundle = a parcel of requests | a tied bundle
ink = berry-black ink | ink thin as tea
cidersteam = the spicy breath | the apple steam
dryrack = a high shelf | the dry ledge
swimstroke = a long easy reach | a quiet stroke
wick = a bit of twisted rush | a rush end
fold = the old crease | the raised fold

any
opinion city for 2 : There's a place in this city for my name. I'm prepared to stand about until somebody finds it.
opinion dole for 2 : A mouth can stay shut about hunger while the belly's writing a petition of its own.
opinion strangers for 1 : A traveller sees the water from the other end. Worth setting down a parcel to hear that.
opinion festivals against 1 : I still owe a day's rent when the day disappears under flags.
opinion houses against 2 : I'd like one House seal beside my own thumbprint. Then we'd see which leaves the greater stain.
opinion sump for 1 : I can ask for dry straw down here without explaining the condition of my roof.

grown
line greet : Greetings. There's clear standing room beside me. | Well met. I can spare these next few minutes.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Early company. The ink isn't even mixed yet.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A new mark in the margin of my day. Welcome.
line greet.return : A greeting duly received, and one for you. | Glad you stopped level with me.
line again.open : Back on the same page, I see.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Over here by my raised paw!
line farewell : Go with enough light to read your way. | I'll leave you to the rest of your errand.
line farewell.return : And an easy passage homeward for you. | My good wishes go along in your pocket.
line react.news : I'll listen before I put a mark beside it. | Take your time over the particulars.
line react.news.new : First wet gleam of that I've seen.
line react.news.known : I've seen the shape of that account already.
line react.news.doubt : I'd want a second copy before swearing to the first.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : I'll gladly mark that day down to remember.
line answer.how : Still turning up. Some days that takes the lot.
line ask.how : Anything come back to you for all your trouble?
line sympathise : Come stand clear of other ears for a bit.
line reassure : Leave yourself a margin. There's room to mend a poor beginning.
line ack : I take your meaning exactly.
line give.advice : I'm keeping the particulars straight.
line refuse : I'm due elsewhere, and the walk takes every spare minute.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=loss|death] : I'd keep the page clear around that name. | Hard news deserves a decent interval of quiet.
line accept_decline : There's no mark against you for choosing otherwise. | You choose how to spend the hour.
line preclose : I ought to start for the next desk before it closes. | I'd better put my feet to my errand.
line accept_preclose : Go on while the road's a little quieter. | You've another page of the day to fill.

scene shadow
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give me a hull's shadow and I'll name what cast it. | I can tell two sister ships apart at noon.
b : What if the bow's behind a wall? | Does the paint show in a shadow?
a : I look for the missing length in the stern. It's like reading half a familiar word. | No, but one casts a little hook where the other's rail runs straight.


scene paper
when topic=work|memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My petition's made more visits to the Office than it has pages. | I've practised asking for #receipt#.
b : Why keep making the walk? | Does that get your request granted?
a : If I do nothing, the answer's settled without me. | I can point to that mark on my next visit.


scene straw
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fresh straw makes the floor sound newly roofed. | I scatter the longest stalks where I get up.
b : A roof under your feet? | Easier to sweep?
a : Just that little dry whisper. I missed it all winter. | Easier to find the floor by feel before daylight.


scene store
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I leave space under the lowest stock. | I stack one parcel with the tie sticking out.
b : What's the empty space for? | Won't that catch on a sleeve?
a : To find the creeping wet before the cloth does. | Better a loose tie than hauling the whole pile apart to open it.


scene swim
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first #swimstroke# always feels too short. | Swimming takes the office dust out of my ears.
b : Do you stretch out the next? | Is the Sound very quiet?
a : I let the water finish carrying me before I reach. | Underneath it is. I spend a moment there before coming up.


scene cider
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I drink cider slowly enough to find the last spice. | My nose gets the first turn at hot cider.
b : Which one stays longest? | And what does your tongue get?
a : The sharp little taste right at the back. I'm still putting a name to it. | The apple underneath when the steam's spent.


scene stamp
when topic=land|work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a spot on my folded paper as round as a seal. | I wrap my request in plain cloth on Office days.
b : Did someone finally sign it? | Why no ribbon?
a : Cider. I'll know a proper seal when one comes. | I haven't any interest in getting the ribbon noticed.


scene smoke
when topic=weather self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Smoke smudges the far bank out of existence. | I save my good copy from the smoke.
b : Still know which way's home? | Doesn't it dry the ink?
a : My feet know perfectly. It's my eyes that begrudge the loss. | It leaves a thumb's worth of grey over every word.


scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd trust #self.friend# with the only copy I had. | I can swim quietly beside a friend.
b : Would you risk it? | No racing?
a : I'd make another first. Trust's no cure for weather. | Best sort of company lets a wolf float.


scene mud
when topic=weather self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Mud took the shape off both my prints. | I walked the long edge round a mudhole.
b : Need prints to find the way back? | Did you arrive clean?
a : I needed dry ankles for the Office. A fine beginning. | Came in late, but nobody had to mop my tracks.


scene rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Big warm drops look like new seals on the water. | I'm leaving the hood down for a minute.
b : How many can you count? | Won't it soak behind your ears?
a : About three before one seal runs into the next. | A warm rain can have that particular liberty.


scene queue
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Once I stood a whole hour behind an empty coat. | I mark a wait by the light on the floor.
b : Someone had left a place in line? | Is that easier than counting?
a : It was on a peg. The room was dark. I went pink to the ears. | There's something to show for it. A whole flagstone passed.


scene market
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When the markets filled with food I learned how much space a sack wants. | I can feel when a parcel's tied too tight.
b : More when full? | Surely tighter keeps it safe?
a : More when near empty. It slumps into its neighbours. | Not if the cord bites through the wrapper before it sells.


scene board
when topic=travel|land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The headland is where I learned to read hulls. | I look back from the headland sometimes.
b : Is that high enough? | At the city?
a : From there I can take in a hull's shadow in a single look. | At the roofs. I like identifying my own from the wrong side.


scene letters
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I practised my name on a wet barrel. | I used to copy the letters off crate ends.
b : With ink? | Can you still read them upside down?
a : A straw. The mark lasted just long enough to judge. | Faster upside down, some days. That's how they were stacked.


scene visit
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like an errand with a landing at each end. | There's always a second walk inside an Office errand.
b : Prefer travelling on water? | From one desk to another?
a : I just like knowing for certain that I've arrived. | Sometimes from one end of a sentence to the other.


scene boss
when topic=work self.boss self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I ask #self.boss# for time away, I name the hour I'll return. | I leave a tidy counter whenever I ask for time away.
b : What if the Office keeps you? | So anyone could take over?
a : I go back to work. There's another week coming. | That's the decent part of asking.


scene home
when topic=home self.street
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #self.street# is the last line on my request. | I could draw the turn home blind.
b : Does an address really matter? | Would a stranger recognise it?
a : An answer can't come back by following a wish. | I'd add the bent gutter. No street has another quite its equal.


story corner [topic=memories]
  : I took a clean sheet uphill in tearing sideways rain.
  : One corner worked free of my coat and took the rain straight on. I unfolded four sheets' worth of matching holes.
  b : Four holes ruined an entire request?
  : I wrote between them. The little wet windows looked out on my own knees.


story eel [topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming]
  : I mistook a trailing weed for the tail of an eel and chased it halfway along the shore.
  : It kept exactly my speed. I'd never met such a courteous eel.
  b : What was pulling it?
  : My ankle. I untied the weed and watched my great rival float away.


story twins [topic=travel]
  : Two hulls went by with equal shadows, and for once I held my tongue.
  : There was a pale gap in one that kept flickering shut. I waited for a clearer patch of sun.
  b : Did that settle their names?
  : It settled their number. I was trying to name one hull and its long reflection.


rule @stock
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry goods up a shelf, please. | Leave me the cord. I'll use that bit again.


rule @wait
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A good clean sheet of a morning. | Light enough to read the smallest hand.


rule @smell
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Rain's laid the dust on my copy. | The ink can wait under my coat.


rule @sound
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's a shape I'd recognise stripped of sail. | I can put a hull to that shadow.

dlg resident.hub : I've a little time between errands. Spend it carefully.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your last words have kept their outline.
dlg resident.job [self.job=merchant] : My work takes me to #self.workplace#. Things come in tied and go out measured.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : My pen kept this much: #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The claim was this. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'd leave a margin for error.
dlg resident.bye : Put your important papers somewhere dry.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : We'll have to do our reading by ear tonight.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Let's keep the particulars short enough to write on a slip.
dlg resident.job : I carry each small task through and make a mark when it's done.

graft resident.hub
choice Why carry two copies of a petition? -> office_copy
node office_copy
say One for the desk and one to show what I left there. I started out believing a single sheet would be enough.
free
choice What do you want back from the desk? -> office_copy_more
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node office_copy_more
say A day and a mark. Even an unwelcome answer would have some edges I could get hold of.
choice I'll leave you some room. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
